description:
Write a record whose items live in a flexible array member, in a single allocation:

```c
struct scores
{
    size_t count;
    char name[16];       /* zero-terminated; longer names are cut to 15 characters */
    int values[];
};

struct scores *scores_new(const char *name, const int *values, size_t count);   /* NULL if malloc fails */
int scores_best(const struct scores *s);                  /* the largest value, or 0 when count is 0 */
struct scores *scores_add(struct scores *s, int value);   /* grows with realloc and appends; returns
                                                             the new pointer, or NULL (s unchanged) on failure */
size_t scores_bytes(size_t count);                        /* how many bytes a record of count values needs */
```

The caller frees the record with `free`.

